  - { id: rp_jar_nina, kind: reply, layer: 2, topic: the_jar, partner: nina, text: "Your jar stays on the top shelf, away from my starter. Don't take it personally. I don't trust anybody's for the first week." }
  - { id: rp_bread_tomas, kind: reply, layer: 2, topic: the_bread, partner: tomas, text: "Bread? I can only tell you one useful thing. Turn the trays at twenty minutes, because Nina's left oven runs cold." }
  - { id: rp_bread_tomas_b, kind: reply, layer: 2, topic: the_bread, partner: tomas, text: "Don't ask me about shaping, because I only ever did the ovens. Nina's the one with the hands for it." }
  - { id: rp_bread_tomas_c, kind: reply, layer: 2, topic: the_bread, partner: tomas, text: "Flour your hands more than you think you need to. That's the only shaping advice Nina ever gave me." }
  - { id: rp_bread_nina, kind: reply, layer: 2, topic: the_bread, partner: nina, text: "Here's my advice. Shape it as if you're cross with it, then forgive it once it's in the oven." }
  - { id: rp_boat_elena, kind: reply, layer: 2, topic: the_boat, partner: elena, text: "She needs her hull scraped and a great deal of patience. I've already bought the scraper." }
  - { id: rp_boat_tomas, kind: reply, layer: 2, topic: the_boat, partner: tomas, text: "It's a boat, that's all. There's not much to tell you." }
  - { id: rp_boat_nina, kind: reply, layer: 2, topic: the_boat, partner: nina, text: "That's their dad's boat. Ask Elena or Tomas about it, not me." }
  - { id: rp_abt_elena, kind: reply, layer: 2, topic: about_tomas, partner: elena, text: "Tomas is always fine, apparently. He'd tell you he was fine if he was on fire." }
  - { id: rp_abt_nina, kind: reply, layer: 2, topic: about_tomas, partner: nina, text: "He had the best hands I ever trained, and now they're wasted on fish." }
  - { id: rp_abe_nina, kind: reply, layer: 2, topic: about_elena, partner: nina, text: "Elena? She talks enough for three people. She means about half of it, but it's the right half." }
  - { id: rp_count_elena, kind: reply, layer: 2, topic: the_count, partner: elena, text: "I count everyone who buys a one-way ticket into town, and everyone who buys one out. This year more people have come to stay than have left, so don't jinx it." }
